<Text>% Calculate Gain factor so that the RMS value of the signal at the &#x000D;&#x000A;% input of the modulator is sqrt( RF_Power * 2 * RefR );&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;GainForSignalWithRMSOf1=sqrt(RF_Power*2*RefR);&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;% Account for the fact that the rms value of the IQ signal at the&#x000D;&#x000A;% output of the PAM_Mappers is &#x000D;&#x000A;%&#x000D;&#x000A;% sqrt( 1/4 * ( 1^2 + (-1)^2 + (1/3)^2 + (-1/3)^2 ) * 2 )&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;PAM_RMS = sqrt( ( 1 + 1 + 1/9 + 1/9 ) * 2 / 4 );&#x000D;&#x000A;&#x000D;&#x000A;Gain = GainForSignalWithRMSOf1 / PAM_RMS;&#x000D;&#x000A;</Text>
<UnitUse><T>Int</T><D>2</D></UnitUse>
<Item XName="BPMgr" Type="BPMgr">
<BPLines><T>Empty</T></BPLines>
<BPStates><T>Empty</T></BPStates></Item>
<Item XName="EqnBlock" Type="EqnBlock">
<Lang><T>Int</T><D>1</D></Lang></Item>
<Item XName="Font" Type="Font">
